{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "02335",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 0.82,
      "end_seconds": 6.34,
      "duration_seconds": 5.52,
      "text": "Hello, take a seat, I'll be with you in a second."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 7.29,
      "end_seconds": 10.34,
      "duration_seconds": 3.05,
      "text": "Hello, thanks for fitting me in."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 12.33,
      "end_seconds": 15.67,
      "duration_seconds": 3.34,
      "text": "Was it a long journey this morning?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 19.97,
      "end_seconds": 23.99,
      "duration_seconds": 4.02,
      "text": "Not too bad, the roads were quiet."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 25.14,
      "end_seconds": 28.05,
      "duration_seconds": 2.91,
      "text": "What do you need help with?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 28.57,
      "end_seconds": 33.13,
      "duration_seconds": 4.56,
      "text": "I wanted to get a red swollen foot looked at."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 34.06,
      "end_seconds": 37.21,
      "duration_seconds": 3.15,
      "text": "How long has it been like this?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 39.2,
      "end_seconds": 41.14,
      "duration_seconds": 1.94,
      "text": "Probably four weeks. Yeah."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 42.39,
      "end_seconds": 45.19,
      "duration_seconds": 2.8,
      "text": "Is there anything else with it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 46.52,
      "end_seconds": 59.17,
      "duration_seconds": 12.65,
      "text": "An ulcer under the big toe goes along with it, most of the time. The ulcer under the big toe? That's been for one week."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 75.37,
      "end_seconds": 81.59,
      "duration_seconds": 6.22,
      "text": "A few quick ones: tracking redness, black skin, fever or pain in the foot?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 83.06,
      "end_seconds": 89.03,
      "duration_seconds": 5.97,
      "text": "No, no tracking redness, black skin, fever or pain in the foot."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 89.88,
      "end_seconds": 92.79,
      "duration_seconds": 2.91,
      "text": "How are your bowels, any trouble?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 96.07,
      "end_seconds": 98.14,
      "duration_seconds": 2.07,
      "text": "No, all normal there."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 99.75,
      "end_seconds": 103.45,
      "duration_seconds": 3.7,
      "text": "Alright, how are your joints, any aches elsewhere?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 104.37,
      "end_seconds": 106.07,
      "duration_seconds": 1.7,
      "text": "Nothing else aches."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 106.87,
      "end_seconds": 109.81,
      "duration_seconds": 2.94,
      "text": "A few questions about your lifestyle now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 110.4,
      "end_seconds": 123.96,
      "duration_seconds": 13.56,
      "text": "Not much, I mostly stay in these days. I'm a hairdresser, on my feet all day. I drink a lot of tea and snack through the day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 138.46,
      "end_seconds": 143.51,
      "duration_seconds": 5.05,
      "text": "Are you allergic to anything? Any allergies to medicines or foods?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 144.62,
      "end_seconds": 149.03,
      "duration_seconds": 4.41,
      "text": "I'm allergic to naproxen, I get a rash."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 150.02,
      "end_seconds": 154.34,
      "duration_seconds": 4.32,
      "text": "Any inherited conditions that you know of in the family?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 155.81,
      "end_seconds": 159.15,
      "duration_seconds": 3.34,
      "text": "My mother has an underactive thyroid."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 175.88,
      "end_seconds": 178.72,
      "duration_seconds": 2.84,
      "text": "Have you had any previous surgeries?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 180.35,
      "end_seconds": 182.07,
      "duration_seconds": 1.72,
      "text": "No surgery, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 194.52,
      "end_seconds": 197.07,
      "duration_seconds": 2.55,
      "text": "Do you take any regular medication?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 197.84,
      "end_seconds": 198.88,
      "duration_seconds": 1.04,
      "text": "No, none."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 203.61,
      "end_seconds": 207.45,
      "duration_seconds": 3.84,
      "text": "Any medical conditions, anything you've been treated for?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 210.01,
      "end_seconds": 212.55,
      "duration_seconds": 2.54,
      "text": "No, um, no conditions."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 216.06,
      "end_seconds": 218.92,
      "duration_seconds": 2.86,
      "text": "Let me take your readings now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 231.43,
      "end_seconds": 233.59,
      "duration_seconds": 2.16,
      "text": "Sit still for a moment..."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 251.5,
      "end_seconds": 259.96,
      "duration_seconds": 8.46,
      "text": "Okay: pulse is 91 beats a minute, BP is 118 over 73. And temperature is 38.5 degrees, saturation 97 percent."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 261.9,
      "end_seconds": 263.55,
      "duration_seconds": 1.65,
      "text": "Is that normal?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 264.47,
      "end_seconds": 267.26,
      "duration_seconds": 2.79,
      "text": "We'll look at it together shortly."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 268.78,
      "end_seconds": 272.78,
      "duration_seconds": 4.0,
      "text": "I'll examine you in a second, make yourself comfortable."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 274.42,
      "end_seconds": 275.86,
      "duration_seconds": 1.44,
      "text": "Does that hurt?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 293.06,
      "end_seconds": 299.49,
      "duration_seconds": 6.43,
      "text": "The ulcer is deep to the fat with surrounding redness and the foot pulses are present."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 304.77,
      "end_seconds": 324.25,
      "duration_seconds": 19.48,
      "text": "All finished, thank you. So where does that leave us? My working impression is an infected diabetic foot ulcer. Just to be sure I understood. You've had a red swollen foot for four weeks, and no tracking redness or black skin."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 325.87,
      "end_seconds": 326.57,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Exactly."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 328.55,
      "end_seconds": 336.48,
      "duration_seconds": 7.93,
      "text": "I'd like to arrange blood tests for infected ulcer. I think a wound swab makes sense here, for infected ulcer."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 338.07,
      "end_seconds": 340.19,
      "duration_seconds": 2.12,
      "text": "Is that done today?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 341.2,
      "end_seconds": 365.83,
      "duration_seconds": 24.63,
      "text": "We'll begin with co-amoxiclav, 625 milligrams, three times a day, seven days. That should help with infected ulcer. I'll put all of this in writing so you don't have to remember it. Keep the weight off the foot and keep the dressing dry. The diabetic foot clinic would be the right next step, I'll refer you."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 366.8,
      "end_seconds": 369.54,
      "duration_seconds": 2.74,
      "text": "Sure, where do I go?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 370.94,
      "end_seconds": 389.44,
      "duration_seconds": 18.5,
      "text": "If it hasn't settled in a month, we'd think about an X-ray of the foot, but not now. One warning sign to remember: the symptoms get worse. In that case don't wait. See me again in two days. Have I covered everything you wanted?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 392.39,
      "end_seconds": 396.26,
      "duration_seconds": 3.87,
      "text": "Right, I'll do that. Thank you, doctor."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 397.92,
      "end_seconds": 399.34,
      "duration_seconds": 1.42,
      "text": "Look after yourself."
    }
  ]
}